    "result_text": "All green. The full build succeeded \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and all 3 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI migrated telephone handling from the old \"10-digit strip\" behaviour to E.164 form.\n\n**New \u2014 shared converter** (`rest/function/owner/E164Telephone.java`): strips spaces, dashes and brackets; keeps a leading `+` and its country code when present, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits; requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else throws `InvalidTelephoneException`. Provides `toE164` (throwing) and `toE164OrNull` (for tolerant comparison of existing data).\n- `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`\n- `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`\n- `12` \u2192 `+6112` (4 digits) \u2192 rejected\n\n**Changed:**\n- `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` \u2014 now stores the E.164 string via the converter instead of a 10-digit number.\n- `EnsureUniqueTelephone` \u2014 detects duplicates by comparing E.164 values (existing owners' telephones are converted the same way, tolerating unparseable seed formats by skipping them).\n- `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2014 message/javadoc updated to the E.164 rule (still 400 via the existing handler).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 the entity's telephone bean-validation was `@Digits(...)` + `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")`, which would have rejected a `+`-prefixed value at JPA save time. Replaced with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (kept `@NotEmpty`, removed the now-unused `@Digits` import).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 the `OwnerFields.telephone` schema (pattern/example/description) now documents the E.164 form, keeping the generated DTO and API docs consistent with what's stored and returned.\n\nPresence checking (`ValidateOwnerRequiredFields`) and the 400/409 escalation wiring were already correct and left unchanged.",
